Part 1: JWT Authentication Implementation Plan
This plan covers only JWT-based authentication with local user registration and login (email/password). No OAuth2 yet.

1. Architecture Overview
Authentication Flow
Registration:
User → POST /auth/register (email, password, name)
     → Server validates input
     → Server hashes password
     → Server creates user in database
     → Server generates JWT tokens
     → Returns { accessToken, refreshToken }

Login:
User → POST /auth/login (email, password)
     → Server validates credentials
     → Server generates JWT tokens
     → Returns { accessToken, refreshToken }

API Request:
User → GET /api/protected (Authorization: Bearer {accessToken})
     → JWT Filter extracts and validates token
     → Sets authentication in SecurityContext
     → Controller processes request

Token Refresh:
User → POST /auth/refresh (refreshToken)
     → Server validates refresh token
     → Server generates new access token
     → Returns { accessToken }

